# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Every real route is prerendered as a flat file by scripts/prerender.mjs
# (dist/catalog.html, dist/book/<id>.html, dist/news/<slug>.html, ...), which
# Cloudflare Pages serves extensionless at HTTP 200 — so the URL that Google
# crawls is byte-identical to the sitemap <loc> and the canonical tag. No SPA
# fallback rewrite is needed.
#
# The only rule left is the 404: because dist/404.html exists, Pages' SPA mode
# (which would otherwise soft-404 unknown URLs into the homepage) is disabled,
# and unknown paths return a real 404 instead.

/*   /404.html   404
